.TH PMASK 1 "2026" "pmask 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pmask \- run a process or process tree with a redacted /proc entry
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pmask
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.br
.B pmask
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fB\-\-args\-from\-fd\fR \fIN\fR
.br
.B pmask
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fB\-\-image\fR \fIPATH\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.br
.B pmask
\fB\-\-explain\fR [\fB\-\-profile\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-label\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
.br
.B pmask
\fB\-\-audit\fR [\fB\-\-pid\fR \fIPID\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-observer\fR \fIROLE\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
.br
.B pmask
\fB\-\-profile\-json\fR [\fB\-\-pid\fR \fIPID\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-label\fR \fINAME\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pmask
redacts Linux
.B /proc
metadata
.RB ( cmdline ,
.BR environ ,
.BR comm ,
and
.BR AT_EXECFN )
for a single process or an entire process tree while each program keeps its real
.B argv
and
.BR envp .
Every other local account sees only the presentation label, and in the default profiles
.RB ( auto ,
.BR single ,
.BR tree ,
and
.BR tee )
same-uid observers are denied
.BR environ ,
.BR maps ,
.BR auxv ,
.BR exe ,
.BR fd ,
.BR cwd ,
and
.B /proc/\fIpid\fB/mem
with
.B EACCES
via
.BR PR_SET_DUMPABLE=0 .
.PP
In the
.B single
profile (selected automatically by
.B \-\-profile auto
for direct native ELF binaries), a transient double-forked helper seizes the process for its
.B execve
entry and completion stops, completes the redaction in place, cleans up any staged carrier, and detaches and exits immediately.
The payload runs in its original PID with zero persistent supervisor,
.BR "TracerPid: 0" ,
.BR "Threads: 1" ,
.BR "Seccomp: 0" ,
and
.BR "NoNewPrivs: 0" .
.PP
In the
.B tree
profile (selected automatically for shells, launchers,
.B #!
scripts, and tree flags), a single-threaded supervisor
.RB ( "Threads: 1" )
tracks every descendant process across forks and execs.
At the
.B execve
entry stop, the tracer rewrites the argument and environment pointer arrays of the old image so the kernel never copies the real command line into the new image of an ELF target.
At the exec completion stop, the tracer writes the real strings into an anonymous
.B MADV_DONTDUMP
mapping inside the tracee, restores the inline arrays, installs a minimal decoy environment (110 bytes as root with
.BR HOME=/root ,
or 109 bytes as non-root with
.BR HOME=/tmp :
.BR PATH ,
.BR HOME ,
.BR LANG ,
and
.BR TERM ,
truncated to complete entries only if the kernel window is smaller),
and relocates the kernel windows inside
.B [stack]
via
.BR prctl(PR_SET_MM_MAP) .
.PP
Profile ranking: use
.B single
(#1 default for direct native ELF binaries: zero persistent supervisor,
.BR "TracerPid: 0" ),
.B tree
for shells, scripts, and multi-process trees,
.BR pmaskd (8)
with
.B \-\-run\-as\-uid
(or a dedicated host uid) to eliminate same-uid
.B EACCES
signals, and
.B tee
for fail-closed user, pid, and mount namespaces with a private
.BR /proc .
.PP
Honest scope:
.B pmask
targets a same-uid local observer without root.
Root on the host,
.BR CAP_SYS_PTRACE ,
kernel modules, hypervisors, and hardware enclaves are out of scope.
.SH PROFILES
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " NAME"
Select an execution and stealth profile:
.RS
.TP
.B auto
(default) Selects
.B single
for direct native ELF binaries, and
.B tree
for shells, launchers
.RB ( sh ,
.BR bash ,
.BR env ,
.BR make ,
.BR xargs ,
and similar),
.B #!
scripts, and tree-only flags.
.TP
.B single
In-place masked exec with a transient helper: zero persistent supervisor,
.BR "TracerPid: 0" ,
.BR "Threads: 1" ,
no extra seccomp filters or
.BR NoNewPrivs ,
and profile defaults of
.B \-\-rexec
.RB ( \-\-rexec\-mode=auto )
and
.BR \-\-no\-dumpable
(the transient helper exits before
.B main()
runs; pass
.B \-\-encrypt\-memory
to seal even that brief window).
Refuses tree-only flags
.RB ( \-\-stealth ,
.BR \-\-watch\-rename ,
.BR \-\-exec\-once ,
.BR \-\-hide\-pid ,
.BR \-\-daemon ,
.BR \-\-report ,
.BR \-\-secret\-close\-on\-exec ,
.BR \-\-isolate ,
.BR \-\-unshare ,
.BR \-\-follow ,
.BR \-\-no\-follow ,
.BR \-\-parent\-label ,
.BR \-\-audit ,
and non-\fBdetach\fR
.BR \-\-on\-exit )
with exit 255.
.TP
.B tree
Single-threaded supervisor
.RB ( "Threads: 1" )
covering forks, shells, scripts, and descendants, with profile defaults of
.B \-\-rexec
.RB ( \-\-rexec\-mode=auto
for ELF targets),
.BR \-\-no\-dumpable ,
and
.BR \-\-encrypt\-memory .
.TP
.B tee
Composes redaction with user, pid, and mount namespaces and a private
.B /proc
(plus private
.B /tmp
by default) and normalizes
.B cwd
to
.BR / .
Fails closed with exit 255 whenever unprivileged user namespaces or the private
.B /proc
mount are refused, or when combined with
.B \-\-no\-redact
or
.BR \-\-isolate=none .
.TP
.B compat
Legacy v0.1.0 flag-driven defaults: tree supervision, dumpable by default, no forced
.BR \-\-rexec ,
and no forced
.BR \-\-encrypt\-memory .
.RE
.TP
.B \-\-auto
Alias for
.B "\-\-profile auto"
(the default).
.TP
.B \-\-follow
Follow and redact all descendants (selects
.B tree
mode; inverse of
.BR \-\-no\-follow ).
.TP
.B \-\-reparent
In
.B single
profile, double-fork the masked payload so it runs reparented to PID 1 (or the nearest subreaper) and exit 0 once the masked exec completes and detaches.
Refused outside
.B single
profile (exit 255).
.TP
.BI \-\-parent\-label " NAME"
Set a separate presentation label for the supervisor process in
.B tree
mode so the supervisor and payload do not share an identical label pair.
Checked by the same label impersonation policy as
.BR \-\-label .
.TP
.BI \-\-cwd " PATH"
Change the child's working directory to
.I PATH
after resolving
.IR COMMAND ,
normalizing
.BR /proc/\fIpid\fB/cwd .
.TP
.BI \-\-rexec\-mode " MODE"
Choose the
.B \-\-rexec
image carrier:
.B auto
(default) prefers a private 0500 executable inside a private 0700 staging directory and falls back to sealed memfd on noexec mounts;
.B path
uses a private 0500 staged file unlinked immediately at
.B PTRACE_EVENT_EXEC
with zero
.B /memfd:
fingerprint in
.B exe
and
.BR maps ;
.B tmpfile
uses an unnamed
.B O_TMPFILE
executable on an executable mount executed via
.B execveat(AT_EMPTY_PATH)
(zero directory entry ever linked on disk, immune to
.B SIGKILL
at any point, and zero
.B /memfd:
fingerprint);
.B memfd
uses a sealed anonymous
.B memfd_create
carrier.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-rexec
Opt out of profile-default
.B \-\-rexec
image staging.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-impersonation
Allow labels or
.B comm
names that use kernel-thread bracket syntax
.RB ( [...] )
or match critical system service names
.RB ( sshd ,
.BR systemd ,
.BR init ,
.BR cron ,
.BR crond ,
.BR systemd\-journald ,
.BR systemd\-udevd ,
.BR udevd ,
.BR dbus\-daemon ,
.BR polkitd ,
.BR auditd ,
.BR rsyslogd ,
and
.BR syslogd ).
Without this flag, those labels exit 2.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-label " \fINAME\fR"
Set the presentation label.
Pass
.B \-
for a blank label of one space.
The label must not contain NUL, LF, or CR.
Default: the program name with all arguments removed.
Kernel-thread bracket labels and critical daemon names are refused with exit 2 unless
.B \-\-allow\-impersonation
is passed.
.TP
.B \-\-label\-empty
Set an empty presentation label.
.TP
.BI \-\-argv0 " NAME"
Set
.B argv[0]
for the program.
Default: the command string as typed.
.TP
.BI \-\-comm " NAME"
Set the process name shown by
.BR top ,
up to 15 bytes.
Default: the label truncated to 15 bytes.
Subject to the same impersonation policy as
.BR \-\-label .
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-env
Leave
.B /proc/\fIpid\fB/environ
visible.
This option takes no separate argument.
Writing
.B "\-\-keep\-env NAME CMD"
or
.B "\-\-keep\-env NAME \-\- CMD"
where
.I NAME
looks like an environment variable list fails fast with exit 2 and directs you to
.B \-\-keep\-env=NAME
or
.B \-\-
before the command.
.TP
.BI \-\-keep\-env= NAME[,NAME...]
Keep only the named environment variables visible.
Use the inline equals form.
Repeat this option to keep more variables.
.TP
.BI \-\-env " K=V"
Add or replace one environment variable.
Repeat this option to set more variables.
.TP
.BI \-\-env\-file " PATH"
Read environment variables from PATH, one
.B KEY=VALUE
per line.
The parser skips blank lines and lines starting with #, strips trailing CR, and allows an optional
.B export
prefix.
The parser trims surrounding blanks from VALUE, removes one matching pair of single or double quotes, and rejects NUL bytes.
Repeat this option to load multiple files.
.TP
.BI \-\-args\-from\-fd " N"
Read the command from file descriptor N as a NUL-separated vector, program first and arguments next.
This option replaces
.IR COMMAND ,
so do not pass a command after the options.
.B pmask
duplicates the descriptor before reading so the caller's descriptor stays open.
The reader consumes the argument stream and caps it at 8 MiB.
.B pmask
refuses larger vectors without buffering them.
.TP
.BI \-\-on\-exit " POLICY"
Set the policy for descendants still running when the command exits.
.B detach
(default) detaches each settled descendant while keeping its label.
.B wait
supervises the tree until every descendant exits.
.B kill
sends SIGKILL to remaining descendants.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-follow
Redact only the direct child.
The tracer still tracks descendants but does not redact them.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-exit\-kill
Disable
.BR PTRACE_O_EXITKILL .
The process tree survives if the supervisor dies.
The parser and shell completions also accept
.BR \-\-no\-exitkill .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-dumpable
Set
.B PR_SET_DUMPABLE=0
in every process of the tree and on the supervisor.
Same-uid observers receive
.B EACCES
on seven
.B /proc
surfaces:
.BR environ ,
.BR maps ,
.BR auxv ,
.BR exe ,
.BR fd ,
.BR cwd ,
and
.BR mem ,
and the kernel zeroes
.B /proc/\fIpid\fB/stat
fields 48 to 51
.RB ( arg_start
through
.BR env_end ).
Core dumps and debugger attach stop working.
Enabled by default in
.BR single ,
.BR tree ,
and
.B tee
profiles, and for
.B \-\-secret
or
.B \-\-secret\-fd
runs in redaction mode (plain
.B \-\-no\-redact
mode runs without a tracer and sets
.B RLIMIT_CORE=0
instead).
On a host with
.B hidepid=invisible
or
.BR hidepid=ptraceable ,
same-uid observers cannot see a non-dumpable process, so hidden-pid sweepers can flag it.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-dumpable
Keep the payload dumpable, opting out of profile-default or secret-triggered
.BR PR_SET_DUMPABLE=0 .
.TP
.B \-\-strict\-exec
Refuse every exec shape that cannot be redacted at syscall entry.
The tracer kills the tracee with SIGKILL before execution on
.B #!
scripts,
.B vfork
children, settled re-exec bypasses, and any entry-redaction fallback such as a failed memory write or scratch overflow.
.B pmask
refuses
.B \-\-strict\-exec
with
.B \-\-detach
and exits 255.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-foreign
Run a 32-bit (foreign-ABI) image unredacted.
By default,
.B pmask
refuses 32-bit execs before execution because a 32-bit image keeps its real command line, environment, and
.BR comm .
.TP
.B \-\-stealth
Compose the strongest
.B tree
profile shape:
.B \-\-rexec
(using
.BR \-\-rexec\-mode=auto ,
preferring a private staged path over
.B /memfd:
when an executable staging directory is available),
.BR \-\-watch\-rename ,
and
.B \-\-no\-dumpable
unless
.B /proc
uses
.B hidepid=invisible
or
.BR hidepid=ptraceable .
On those mounts,
.B \-\-stealth
keeps the tree dumpable to avoid hidden-pid sweeper alerts and prints that same-uid memory reads stay open.
On standard
.B hidepid=off
mounts,
.B \-\-stealth
applies
.B \-\-no\-dumpable
silently without unsolicited stderr warnings and refuses
.B "\-\-stealth \-\-exec\-once"
with exit 255.
Add
.B \-\-isolate=net
if you also want a private network namespace.
.TP
.B \-\-hide\-pid
Hide the tree's pids from same-uid
.B /proc
readers.
This option is opt-in and never the default.
The kernel mechanism combines
.B PR_SET_DUMPABLE=0
with a
.B /proc
mount using
.B hidepid=invisible
or
.BR hidepid=ptraceable .
.B pmask
refuses weaker mounts,
.BR \-\-no\-follow ,
.BR \-\-detach ,
and
.B \-\-exec\-once
with exit 255.
Hidden pids remain visible to root,
.BR kill(0) ,
.BR pidfd_open ,
cgroupfs
.RB ( cgroup.procs
and
.BR cgroup.threads ),
and non-/proc syscalls such as
.BR getpriority ,
.BR sched_getaffinity ,
and
.BR prlimit .
On
.BR hidepid=ptraceable ,
an already-instantiated inode returns
.B EPERM
instead of
.BR ENOENT .
.TP
.B \-\-encrypt\-memory
Seal at-rest supervisor
.B argv
and
.B environ
copies with XChaCha20-Poly1305.
The per-session key lives in
.B memfd_secret
memory when the kernel supports it, or in
.BR mlock 'ed
heap with a visible note otherwise.
The payload's redaction block stays anonymous and receives
.BR MADV_DONTDUMP .
An anonymous block avoids leaving a
.B /secretmem
VMA fingerprint in the payload.
Payload heap and stack memory remain unencrypted.
Enabled by default in
.B tree
and
.B tee
profiles (in
.BR single ,
the transient helper exits before
.B main()
runs; pass
.B \-\-encrypt\-memory
to seal even that brief window); opt-in only in
.BR compat .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-new\-privs
Set
.B no_new_privs
before exec.
Set-uid binaries and file capabilities then grant no privilege.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-exact
Keep the kernel's original
.B argv
and
.B environ
window extents instead of relocating them.
The tracer overwrites the original argument extent with the label padded by spaces and one trailing NUL.
.B /proc/\fIpid\fB/environ
receives complete non-repeating decoy entries (110 bytes as root with
.BR HOME=/root ,
or 109 bytes as non-root with
.BR HOME=/tmp :
.BR PATH ,
.BR HOME ,
.BR LANG ,
and
.BR TERM ,
truncated to complete entries only if the kernel window is smaller)
or the variables selected by
.BR \-\-keep\-env .
By default, exact mode writes the label, the decoy environment (or kept variables), and
.B AT_EXECFN
inside the kernel
.B [stack]
region via
.BR prctl(PR_SET_MM_MAP) .
.TP
.B \-\-detach
Detach each tracee once its exec completes so
.B TracerPid
reads 0.
Detached processes and their future children run unredacted at later execs.
The session summary counts every detach.
For single native binaries, prefer
.B "\-\-profile single"
(the default under
.BR auto ),
which avoids a persistent supervisor altogether.
.TP
.BI \-\-watch\-rename "[=strict]"
Prevent tracees from changing
.B comm
away from the label.
The seccomp filter traps
.BR prctl(PR_SET_NAME)
plus
.BR open ,
.BR openat ,
.BR openat2 ,
and
.B creat
calls targeting
.BR /proc/.../comm .
The tracer normalizes repeated slashes,
.BR . ,
and
.B ..
before matching paths and denies matching writes with
.BR EACCES .
Pass
.B \-\-watch\-rename=strict
to trap
.BR write ,
.BR writev ,
.BR pwrite64 ,
.BR pwritev ,
and
.B pwritev2
and verify target descriptors via
.BR readlink ,
catching symlink aliases and transferred descriptors.
.B \-\-watch\-rename
implies
.B \-\-no\-new\-privs
and defaults
.B \-\-on\-exit
to
.BR wait .
If filter installation fails, the run exits 126.
.B pmask
refuses
.B \-\-watch\-rename
with
.BR \-\-detach ,
.BR "\-\-on\-exit detach" ,
or
.B "\-\-profile single"
(exit 255) because an unserviced filter returns
.B ENOSYS
in detached descendants.
.PP
Under
.BR \-\-no\-dumpable ,
an unprivileged tracer may fail to reach the label address or read
.B /proc/\fIpid\fB/fd
links inside a non-dumpable tracee.
When label redirection fails, the tracer refuses
.BR prctl(PR_SET_NAME) ,
keeps the label in
.BR comm ,
prints a warning, and counts the refusal.
When
.B readlink
fails with
.B EACCES
on a non-dumpable tracee,
.B pmask
emits one warning per session.
A root tracer retains full access regardless of dumpability.
.TP
.B \-\-rexec
Execute the program from a staged image so
.B /proc/\fIpid\fB/exe
and
.B maps
do not name the real file.
Use
.B \-\-rexec\-mode
to select
.B auto
(default: private 0500 staged path, falling back to sealed memfd on noexec mounts),
.B path
(private 0500 staged file with zero
.B /memfd:
fingerprint),
.B tmpfile
(unnamed
.B O_TMPFILE
executable via
.B execveat(AT_EMPTY_PATH)
with zero directory entry and zero
.B /memfd:
fingerprint), or
.B memfd
(sealed anonymous memfd).
In memfd mode, the child tries carriers in order:
.BR execveat ( AT_EMPTY_PATH ),
then
.BR /proc/self/fd/ N
with
.BR execve ,
then an executable temporary file.
.B pmask
reports and counts every failed carrier step.
Without
.BR \-\-rexec\-allow\-disk ,
image failure exits 126 (or 127 if missing) instead of running the on-disk file.
.TP
.B \-\-rexec\-allow\-disk
Allow the on-disk path as an explicit last resort for
.BR \-\-rexec .
.B pmask
reports and counts the fallback and never enables it automatically.
.TP
.BI \-\-image " PATH"
Read program bytes from PATH without searching
.B PATH
and execute them from a sealed image.
Pass
.B "\-\-image \-"
to read standard input to EOF.
Only ELF binaries work.
Implies
.BR \-\-rexec .
.TP
.BI \-\-image\-from\-fd " N"
Read program bytes from file descriptor N.
The payload receives
.B "<fd image>"
as
.B argv[0]
unless
.B \-\-argv0
overrides it.
Implies
.BR \-\-rexec .
.TP
.B \-\-exec\-once
Reuse one sealed image per distinct program across session execs.
The cache key includes resolved path,
.BR st_dev ,
.BR st_ino ,
.BR ctime ,
.BR mtime ,
size, hugetlb flag, and memfd name.
Later execs use a verified temporary-file carrier, preferring
.B $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
over
.BR /dev/shm .
When
.B PTRACE_O_EXITKILL
is active and
.B \-\-on\-exit
is not
.BR detach ,
the tracer installs an
.BR execve / execveat
seccomp filter so settled tracees run under
.BR PTRACE_CONT .
.B pmask
refuses
.B \-\-exec\-once
with
.BR \-\-no\-dumpable ,
.BR \-\-hide\-pid ,
.B \-\-stealth
on non-hidepid hosts, or a default non-dumpable
.B \-\-secret
session (exit 255).
The cache is unavailable under
.BR \-\-unshare ,
.BR "\-\-redact \-\-isolate" ,
and
.BR \-\-run\-as .
In those cases
.B pmask
prints the reason and runs later execs from disk.
Implies
.BR \-\-rexec .
.TP
.B \-\-hugetlb
Request a hugetlbfs-backed image and report the actual backing.
When huge pages are unavailable,
.B pmask
reports the fallback and uses an ordinary memfd.
Pipe sources from
.B "\-\-image \-"
or
.B \-\-image\-from\-fd
spool first so retry succeeds.
Implies
.BR \-\-rexec .
.TP
.B \-\-unshare
Run inside new user, pid, and mount namespaces with a private
.B /proc
when the kernel permits it.
Otherwise
.B pmask
prints one line and continues without namespaces.
.TP
.BI \-\-scope\-name " NAME"
Re-exec once through
.BR "systemd-run \-\-user \-\-scope" .
.B pmask
sanitizes NAME to letters, digits, dot, underscore, and hyphen up to 64 bytes and names the unit
.BI pmask- NAME \- pid\fR.
The unit description is always the literal
.BR pmask ,
never the command line.
The unit name appears in
.B /proc/\fIpid\fB/cgroup
and
.BR systemctl .
If
.B systemd-run
is unavailable,
.B pmask
prints one line and continues without a scope.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress diagnostics, including the session summary and isolation report.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print every redaction event to stderr.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help "[=\fITOPIC\fR], " \-\-help\-all
Print a concise one-screen overview.
Pass
.B \-\-help=all
or
.B \-\-help\-all
for the complete flag reference, or
.BI \-\-help= TOPIC
(or
.BI "pmask help " TOPIC\fR)
for one section:
.BR profiles ,
.BR redact ,
.BR secrets ,
.BR isolate ,
.BR daemon ,
.BR audit ,
.BR report ,
.BR short ,
or
.BR all .
.SH AUDIT, EXPLAIN, AND PROFILE EXPORT
.TP
.B \-\-explain
Print the named observer
.RB ( "same-uid local observer, no root" ),
explicit non-goals, detected host capabilities (including subuid and helper-uid readiness), hidden surfaces, the
.B EACCES
denial tradeoff, and honest residuals for the selected
.BR \-\-profile ,
then exit 0.
Add
.B \-\-json
for machine-readable output.
.TP
.B \-\-profile\-json
Emit a native
.BR psgen
.B "schema: 2"
JSON profile describing observable process shape (ready to feed directly into
.B psgen
with zero adapter), then exit 0.
With
.BI \-\-pid " PID" ,
probes a live process (including 1-level
.BR children ,
.BR parent ,
and
.B tracer
capture); without
.BR \-\-pid ,
emits a static template for
.B \-\-profile
and
.BR \-\-label .
Never emits raw secret bytes: scrubs explicit tokens from
.B \-\-token\-env
or
.BR \-\-token\-fd ,
sensitive environment keys, and inline secret patterns across every field, recording only
.BR memory.token_present ,
.BR memory.token_sha256 ,
.BR memory.token_len ,
.BR memory.token_charset ,
and
.BR memory.token_placements .
.TP
.B \-\-audit
In standalone mode (with no
.IR COMMAND ,
or with
.BI \-\-pid " PID" ),
probes every
.B /proc
surface plus a bounded full-VMA
.B /proc/\fIpid\fB/mem
scan (up to 64 MiB) against invariants
.B INV\-1
through
.B INV\-10
and exits 0 on pass or 1 on failure.
When invoked with neither
.B \-\-pid
nor
.IR COMMAND ,
runs a self-audit against a live masked child holding a fresh synthetic token on its heap.
Add
.B \-\-json
for deterministic
.B pmask-audit/1
JSON output.
.PP
When combined with
.IR COMMAND ,
prints one residue row per tracee at each exec completion and a final residue count.
Unreadable fields print
.B "not reachable"
instead of zero.
.B pmask
refuses
.B \-\-audit
with
.I COMMAND
outside redact mode, with
.BR "\-\-profile single" ,
or with stdout
.B \-\-report=json
(exit 255).
.TP
.BI \-\-pid " PID"
Target process ID for standalone
.B \-\-audit
or
.BR \-\-profile\-json .
.TP
.BI \-\-observer " ROLE"
Observer perspective for standalone
.BR \-\-audit :
.B same\-uid
(default) or
.BR other\-uid .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit JSON output for
.BR \-\-audit ,
.BR \-\-explain ,
or
.BR \-\-profile\-json .
.TP
.BI \-\-token\-env " VAR"
Read the secret token to hunt during
.B "\-\-audit \-\-pid PID"
or
.B "\-\-profile\-json \-\-pid PID"
from environment variable
.IR VAR .
The variable is removed immediately and never emitted verbatim.
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-token\-fd .
.TP
.BI \-\-token\-fd " N"
Read the secret token to hunt during
.B "\-\-audit \-\-pid PID"
or
.B "\-\-profile\-json \-\-pid PID"
from file descriptor
.IR N .
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-token\-env .
.TP
.BI \-\-real\-exe " PATH"
Expected real executable path to verify is hidden in
.BR exe ,
.BR maps ,
.BR auxv ,
and
.B fd
during
.B "\-\-audit \-\-pid PID"
.RB ( INV\-4 ).
.TP
.BI \-\-real\-cwd " PATH"
Expected real working directory to verify is hidden in
.B cwd
during
.B "\-\-audit \-\-pid PID"
.RB ( INV\-6 ).
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-memfd
Permit
.B /memfd:
executable paths in
.B single
profile during standalone
.B \-\-audit
without failing
.BR INV\-4 .
.SH MODES
.B pmask
selects one of three underlying execution modes before reading any secret.
.TP
.B redact
Default mode where ptrace is permitted.
Redacts
.BR cmdline ,
.BR environ ,
.BR comm ,
and
.B AT_EXECFN
and enforces mask options.
.TP
.B isolate
Run the payload in fresh namespaces without a tracer.
Selected by
.B \-\-isolate
or
.B "\-\-no\-redact \-\-isolate"
when unprivileged user namespaces are available.
No
.B /proc
metadata is redacted.
.TP
.B plain
Run with neither tracer nor namespaces.
Selected by
.BR \-\-no\-redact ,
by hosts that block ptrace, or by
.B \-\-isolate
when both user namespaces and ptrace are unavailable.
.PP
Selection rules:
.B \-\-redact
and
.B \-\-no\-redact
together exit 255.
.B "\-\-redact \-\-isolate=LIST"
redacts the tree inside the named namespaces (used by
.BR "\-\-profile tee" ).
.B \-\-isolate=none
creates no namespace and selects between redact and plain normally.
.B pmask
evaluates
.B \-\-isolate
before ptrace: if user namespaces work, isolation runs even when ptrace is blocked.
If user namespaces fail,
.B pmask
falls back to redact when ptrace works and plain otherwise, printing the probe reason once (except
.BR "\-\-profile tee" ,
which fails closed).
.PP
Tracer-only options do not apply in isolate or plain mode.
These options are
.BR \-\-profile ,
.BR \-\-comm ,
.BR \-\-argv0 ,
.BR \-\-no\-exact ,
.BR \-\-detach ,
.BR \-\-follow ,
.BR \-\-no\-follow ,
.BR \-\-no\-exit\-kill ,
.BR \-\-on\-exit ,
.BR \-\-watch\-rename ,
.BR \-\-unshare ,
.BR \-\-no\-dumpable ,
.BR \-\-strict\-exec ,
.BR \-\-allow\-foreign ,
.BR \-\-parent\-label ,
.BR \-\-reparent ,
.BR \-\-stealth ,
.BR \-\-hide\-pid ,
.BR \-\-encrypt\-memory ,
.BR \-\-audit ,
.BR \-\-secret\-close\-on\-exec ,
and the image family
.RB ( \-\-rexec ,
.BR \-\-rexec\-mode ,
.BR \-\-no\-rexec ,
.BR \-\-rexec\-allow\-disk ,
.BR \-\-image ,
.BR \-\-image\-from\-fd ,
.BR \-\-exec\-once ,
.BR \-\-hugetlb ,
.BR \-\-memfd\-name ).
.B pmask
records each dropped option in stderr notes and in the JSON report.
Six flags fail closed instead of dropping:
.BR \-\-audit ,
.BR \-\-hide\-pid ,
.BR \-\-encrypt\-memory ,
.BR \-\-image ,
.BR \-\-image\-from\-fd ,
and
.B \-\-secret\-close\-on\-exec
when a secret is delivered.
.PP
The label and
.B \-\-label\-empty
apply only in redact mode.
.B \-\-keep\-env
is already satisfied outside redact mode, and
.B \-\-no\-new\-privs
is satisfied in isolate mode.
.BR \-\-env ,
.BR \-\-env\-file ,
.BR \-\-cwd ,
.BR \-\-secret ,
.BR \-\-secret\-fd ,
and
.B \-\-scope\-name
apply in every mode.
In modes without
.BR \-\-no\-dumpable ,
the JSON field
.B payload_dumpable
reflects whether the selected mode left the payload dumpable.
.SH SECRET SIDE
These options and subcommands work without ptrace, except
.BR \-\-secret\-close\-on\-exec ,
which requires the tracer and fails in plain or isolate mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-secret\-fd " [NAME=]N"
Keep caller-opened file descriptor
.I N
open across exec at its existing number (clearing
.BR FD_CLOEXEC )
and export
.B PMASK_SECRET_FD=N
(first unnamed fd) or
.B PMASK_SECRET_<NAME>=N
(named) in the payload's real environment.
Repeatable.
Validates that
.I N
is open before exec (exit 2 if invalid or closed).
Enables
.B \-\-no\-dumpable
in redaction mode unless
.B \-\-allow\-dumpable
is passed (plain
.B \-\-no\-redact
mode runs without a tracer and sets
.B RLIMIT_CORE=0
instead).
Works in
.BR single ,
.BR tree ,
.BR tee ,
.BR compat ,
isolate, and plain modes.
.TP
.BI \-\-secret " NAME=SRC"
Deliver a secret on file descriptor 3, 4, and upward.
The child receives the descriptor number in environment variable
.BR PMASK_SECRET_<NAME> .
.B pmask
upper-cases NAME and replaces every non-alphanumeric ASCII byte with an underscore.
Colliding names fail before any secret loads.
SRC is
.BR file: PATH ,
.BR env: VAR ,
.BR agent: NAME ,
.BR stdin ,
or
.BR literal: VAL .
Repeat this option to deliver multiple secrets.
.PP
In redact mode,
.B \-\-secret
sets
.B \-\-no\-dumpable
on both the payload tree and supervisor by default.
Pass
.B \-\-allow\-dumpable
to opt out.
A
.B literal:
or
.B env:
source still appears in
.BR pmask 's
own argv or environment before self-masking, where kernel audit logs
.RB ( type=EXECVE
and
.BR type=PROCTITLE ),
wrappers, and shell history can record it.
Use
.BR \-\-secret\-fd ,
.BR file: ,
.BR agent: ,
or
.B stdin
with
.B \-\-args\-from\-fd
to keep secrets off the command line.
Delivered descriptors survive exec and pass to descendants unless
.B \-\-secret\-close\-on\-exec
is set.
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " PATH"
Set the secret-agent socket for
.B agent: NAME
sources.
.TP
.BI \-\-isolate "[=LIST]"
Run the payload in fresh user, mount, UTS, IPC, and cgroup namespaces.
.B LIST
selects optional axes:
.BR pid ,
.BR net ,
.BR tmp ,
.BR all
(default), or
.BR none .
.B none
creates no namespaces and keeps host namespaces and
.BR no_new_privs .
When user namespaces are unavailable,
.B pmask
reports the unavailable axis and falls back to redact or plain mode.
.PP
The private
.B /dev
provides
.BR /dev/null ,
.BR /dev/zero ,
.BR /dev/full ,
.BR /dev/random ,
.BR /dev/urandom ,
.BR /dev/tty ,
a private
.BR /dev/shm ,
and
.B /dev/pts
plus
.B /dev/ptmx
when available.
Missing device entries are reported and counted as degradations.
.TP
.B \-\-redact
Request
.B /proc
redaction explicitly (default).
Combine with
.B \-\-isolate=LIST
to redact inside those exact namespaces.
If the host cannot grant LIST,
.B pmask
reports a degradation without substituting a different set.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-redact
Skip
.B /proc
redaction even when ptrace is available.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-argv\-secret
Allow a
.B literal:
or
.B env:
secret in a non-redacting mode and print a disclosure warning instead of refusing the run.
.TP
.B \-\-secret\-burn
Omit
.B F_SEAL_SHRINK
on delivered descriptors so the reader can truncate the secret to zero after reading.
The reader still cannot grow or overwrite the descriptor.
.TP
.B \-\-secret\-close\-on\-exec
Close delivered secret descriptors in every direct child of the payload at fork.
The payload keeps the descriptor across its own exec.
Processes sharing the payload's descriptor table
.RB ( clone(CLONE_FILES)
without
.BR CLONE_THREAD )
cannot be closed safely and are reported as a degradation.
With
.BR \-\-detach ,
enforcement stops below detached tracees and
.B pmask
prints a warning.
.TP
.BI \-\-secret\-fd\-name " NAME"
Name delivered secret memfds NAME instead of
.BR pmask\-secret .
NAME must be 1 to 200 printable bytes with no slash, control byte, or DEL.
Content and seals stay unchanged.
.TP
.BI \-\-memfd\-name " NAME"
Name image memfds and temporary-file carrier tags NAME instead of the sanitized label.
Applies to
.BR \-\-rexec ,
.BR \-\-image ,
.BR \-\-image\-from\-fd ,
.BR \-\-exec\-once ,
and
.BR \-\-hugetlb .
Runs that prepare no image print a warning.
.TP
.BI \-\-report " json"
Print a single JSON report object on stdout after the payload exits.
Use
.B \-\-report\-file
or
.B \-\-report\-fd
to keep payload stdout separate from the JSON document.
.B text
and
.B plain
exit 255.
Refused with
.B \-\-daemon
or explicit
.B "\-\-profile single"
(exit 255).
.TP
.BI \-\-report\-file " PATH"
Write the JSON report to PATH and imply
.BR \-\-report=json .
.B pmask
stages the report via
.B O_TMPFILE
or a mode 0600 temporary file and links or renames it to PATH after the session ends.
.B pmask
refuses symlinks at PATH, sets mode 0600, validates the directory before starting the payload, and exits 255 on write failure.
.TP
.BI \-\-report\-fd " N"
Write the JSON report to open descriptor N (3 or higher).
.B pmask
duplicates N with
.BR O_CLOEXEC .
Descriptors 0, 1, 2, or closed descriptors exit 255 before starting the payload.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B run " [OPTIONS] [--] CMD"
Run a command using the same option parser as default mode.
.TP
.B read " NAME"
Print a secret delivered to this process by
.BR run .
Each descriptor supports one read because inheritors share the file offset.
.TP
.B store " <sub>"
Manage the encrypted store:
.BR init ,
.BR set\ NAME ,
.BR get\ NAME ,
.BR list ,
.BR rm\ NAME ,
and
.BR path .
Options:
.BI \-\-store " PATH"
(default
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/pmask/store.enc ),
.BI \-\-passphrase\-file " P" ,
and
.BI \-\-from\-file " P"
for
.BR set .
Exit status: 0 on success, 1 when the store holds no secret under that name, and 255 on usage, store, or passphrase errors.
.TP
.B agent " [OPTIONS]"
Hold the unlocked store in memory and serve secrets over a Unix socket.
Options:
.BI \-\-store " PATH" ,
.BI \-\-socket " PATH" ,
.BI \-\-passphrase\-file " P" ,
and repeatable
.BI \-\-allow " EXE"
(exact executable path allow-list).
.TP
.B get " NAME [--socket P]"
Request one secret from a running agent.
.TP
.B probe " [--json]"
Report host capabilities per mechanism.
Pass
.B \-\-json
for machine-readable output.
.TP
.B doctor " [--json] [--require LIST]"
Report store status, agent status, and host guarantee verdict.
LIST accepts
.BR redact ,
.BR exact ,
.BR isolate ,
.BR secret\-mem ,
.BR mlock ,
.BR no\-new\-privs ,
.BR non\-dumpable ,
.BR hidepid ,
.BR hide\-pid ,
.BR encrypt\-memory ,
and
.BR landlock .
Exit status: 0 when all requested guarantees are active, 3 when any is degraded, 4 when any is unavailable, and 255 on unknown guarantee names.
.TP
.BR help " [\fITOPIC\fR], " version
Print concise overview, a single help topic
.RB ( profiles ,
.BR redact ,
.BR secrets ,
.BR isolate ,
.BR daemon ,
.BR audit ,
.BR report ,
.BR short ,
or
.BR all ),
or version.
.SH ALIASES
.BR \-a " (= \-\-label), " \-a\-
(= \-l\-),
.BR \-E " (= \-\-keep\-env), " \-F " (= \-\-no\-follow), " \-K " (= \-\-no\-exit\-kill)."
.B pmask
accepts
.B \-f
and
.B \-c
for compatibility with no effect.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PMASK_NO_SELFMASK
Disable redaction of the supervisor's own
.B /proc
entry.
Use only for debugging because the supervisor's command line then stays visible.
.SH LABEL LIMITS
Three layers bound label length.
.B comm
keeps up to 15 bytes.
Exec-entry scratch keeps up to 254 bytes until exec completes.
In-place redaction (when the window is not relocated) truncates the label to the kernel's copied argument span.
.PP
In default exact mode, exec completion writes the full label into the presentation block and relocates the kernel window so settled processes show the whole label.
Under
.B \-\-no\-exact
or a refused
.BR PR_SET_MM_MAP ,
the label stays truncated to the original span.
.B pmask
prints one warning (unless
.BR \-\-quiet )
when a label exceeds 254 bytes.
.SH SESSION SUMMARY
When any exec degrades,
.B pmask
prints one line on stderr:
.PP
.RS
pmask: \fIN\fR of \fIM\fR execs degraded (\fIreasons\fR)
.RE
.PP
Reasons include
.BR post\-exec ,
.BR reexec ,
.BR unredacted ,
.BR comm\-not\-set ,
.BR foreign\-arch ,
and
.BR foreign\-refused ,
with
.BI x K
counts when a reason occurs more than once.
Only
.B unredacted
indicates that real strings may have stayed visible.
.PP
Up to nine additional
.B pmask:
lines appear when their counters are non-zero:
.PP
.RS
.I N
vfork child(ren) took the post-exec path; the \-\-exec\-once cache tag is not applied there
.br
.I N
32-bit (foreign ABI) exec(s) refused; a 32-bit image cannot be redacted, so it is not run unless \-\-allow\-foreign is set
.br
.I N
of
.I M
execs kept the kernel's argv and environ windows (PR_SET_MM_MAP refused)
.br
.I N
tracee(s) left detached after their exec (\-\-detach: their later execs are not redacted)
.br
.I N
tracee(s) stayed dumpable (PR_SET_DUMPABLE refused); \-\-hide\-pid is not active for them
.br
.I N
redaction block(s) could not be marked MADV_DONTDUMP; a core dump could include the block
.br
.I N
secret descriptor(s) could not be closed in a descendant
.br
.I N
\-\-rexec fallback step(s) taken (\fIK\fR used the on-disk last resort)
.br
.I N
rename(s) refused because the label address was not available (comm kept the label)
.RE
.PP
.B \-\-quiet
suppresses all summary lines.
.SH DAEMON MODE
Pass
.BI \-\-daemon " PATH"
to run the job through
.BR pmaskd (8).
The daemon owns the environment and masking policy.
Mask options other than
.B \-\-label
and
.B \-\-label\-empty
have no effect and emit a warning.
.B pmask
refuses
.BR \-\-secret ,
.BR \-\-secret\-fd ,
.BR \-\-isolate ,
.BR \-\-no\-redact ,
.BR \-\-hide\-pid ,
.BR \-\-encrypt\-memory ,
.BR \-\-image ,
.BR \-\-image\-from\-fd ,
.BR \-\-report ,
.BR \-\-report\-file ,
.BR \-\-report\-fd ,
.BR "\-\-profile single" ,
and
.B "\-\-profile tee"
with exit 255 in daemon mode.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B payload
The supervised command's exit status (0 to 255) passes through untouched in local and daemon modes.
When a signal kills the command,
.B pmask
re-raises that signal.
.TP
.B 125
The child failed to install a delivered secret descriptor.
.TP
.B 126
The
.B \-\-rexec
image failed, ptrace was refused in
.B single
profile, or the
.B \-\-watch\-rename
filter could not be installed.
.TP
.B 127
The image was missing or the program could not execute.
.TP
.B 1
Standalone
.B \-\-audit
failed one or more invariants, the requested secret does not exist
.RB ( "store get" ,
.BR "store rm" ,
.BR "pmask read" ,
.BR "pmask get" ),
or the secret descriptor in
.B pmask read
is unreadable.
.TP
.B 2
Label impersonation policy refusal (kernel-thread
.B [...]
or critical daemon name without
.BR \-\-allow\-impersonation ),
space-form
.B \-\-keep\-env NAME
trap, invalid or closed
.BR \-\-secret\-fd ,
missing or unreadable
.B \-\-token\-env
or
.BR \-\-token\-fd ,
or
.B pmask read
refusing to print a secret to a terminal without
.BR \-\-tty .
.TP
.B "3, 4"
.B pmask doctor
found a requested guarantee degraded (3) or unavailable (4).
.TP
.B 255
Usage errors, option refusals, unknown guarantees, unreadable stores, and wrong or missing passphrases.
A
.B pmask:
stderr prefix and the absence of a report distinguish a refusal from a payload returning 255.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pmaskd (8)
